        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177507094?u=02fca01b2bde41566660e171c995c01443421086&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>

<p dir="auto">The content of this PR is a result of what I understood from <a class="user-mention notranslate" data-hovercard-type="user" data-hovercard-url="/users/chrisdavidmills/hovercard" data-octo-click="hovercard-link-click" data-octo-dimensions="link_type:self" href="https://github.com/chrisdavidmills">@chrisdavidmills</a> <a href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42208#pullrequestreview-3534226479" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/pull/42208/hovercard">comment</a></p>
<h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>

<p dir="auto">Adding a note to inform the learners of the rarity of using that technique (<em>preceding pseudo-codes with <code class="notranslate">*</code> for readability improvement</em> ) in real code, and also that that syntax is not adopted in MDN docs.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>

<ul dir="auto">
<li>To give an idea about the usage of that syntax in real code.</li>
<li>To avoid PRs that suggests adopting it, PRs similar to  <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3689332967" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42208" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/pull/42208/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42208">#42208</a> .</li>
</ul>
