        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Improve `typeof undefined` docs]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42207</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42207"/>
        <updated>2025-12-03T06:22:20.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46635587?u=b07ca7dea8057b32559bd35a0303b0f08f865478&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">Clarify how lexical declarations interact with <code class="notranslate">typeof undefined</code> checks when not initialized.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">The <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/undefined#typeof_operator_and_undefined" rel="nofollow">current docs on <code class="notranslate">undefined</code></a> aren't clear about the fact that variables created with <code class="notranslate">let</code> and <code class="notranslate">const</code> will throw a <code class="notranslate">ReferenceError</code> if they're compared using <code class="notranslate">typeof undefined</code> before initialization.</p>]]></content>
