        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Change canvas id to myCanvas in Path2D examples (Fixes #42155)]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42159</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42159"/>
        <updated>2025-11-28T20:12:42.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/162419614?u=2b6e602f394a737b5c7baed1bfb34376d6de6b78&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>

<h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">This PR updates the <code class="notranslate">&lt;canvas&gt;</code> element ID used in the Path2D examples.<br>
The previous examples used <code class="notranslate">id="canvas"</code>, which can lead beginners to accidentally use a non-canvas element with the same ID, resulting in the common error:</p>
<p dir="auto"><code class="notranslate">getContext is not a function</code></p>
<p dir="auto">The examples now consistently use <code class="notranslate">id="myCanvas"</code>.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">Using a more specific and less generic ID helps prevent confusion for new developers.<br>
It avoids accidental misuse of <code class="notranslate">&lt;div id="canvas"&gt;</code> and improves the clarity and reliability of the example code.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Updated the HTML <code class="notranslate">&lt;canvas&gt;</code> ID in both examples.</li>
<li>Updated corresponding JavaScript <code class="notranslate">getElementById()</code> calls.</li>
</ul>
<h3 dir="auto">Related issues and pull requests</h3>
<p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #42155.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3673193420" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42155" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/42155/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42155">#42155</a></p>]]></content>
